```
If `control` is present, `cell_length` is 0. If `cut` is 0, it returns `(segment, _Segment("", style, control))`. If `cut` > 0, it also returns that.

But if `control` is present, the segment is considered to have 0 width.

The issue linked is https://github.com/Textualize/textual/issues/5090. I don't have access to the internet, but the title is "Segment.split_cells fix".

